# DRAFT - what `gcloud builds submit` may upload (deploy/gcp/README.md, step 6).
# Pass it explicitly: gcloud builds submit --ignore-file=deploy/gcp/.gcloudignore ...
# gcloud uploads the source to the Cloud Build staging bucket
# (gs://PROJECT_ID_cloudbuild/source/) BEFORE any .dockerignore applies, so this
# file is what keeps secrets off Google's side. Same allowlist as
# deploy/gcp/Dockerfile.dockerignore, plus the Dockerfile and the build config.
# Run builds from a clean clone, never from the prod working directory.
# Dry check: README.md step 6, "Before the first upload".

/*
!/go.mod
!/go.sum
!/*.go
!/internal/
!/frontend/
!/scoutanalytics.sql
!/deploy/
/deploy/*
!/deploy/gcp/
/deploy/gcp/*
!/deploy/gcp/Dockerfile
!/deploy/gcp/Dockerfile.dockerignore
!/deploy/gcp/cloudbuild.yaml

*_test.go
testdata/

# secrets and private data (never uploaded, whatever the rules above say)
.env
.env.*
scout.session.json
*.session.json
scoutanalytics_data/
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
gcp-*.json
*-key.json
ml/
models/
ml-results/
.claude/
.git/
*.csv

# no JSON at all (keys, session files, exports); the build needs none
*.json
